# tests/test_issue31_turn_state_bundle_b_second_remediation.py is one of two
# files in this repository historically committed with mixed CRLF/LF line
# endings (see its own in-file comments). `git diff --check` treats a
# trailing CR as whitespace by default, which flags every touched line in
# that file regardless of content. This scopes the whitespace check off for
# that one path rather than normalizing its line endings, which would
# rewrite unrelated pre-existing lines.
tests/test_issue31_turn_state_bundle_b_second_remediation.py -whitespace

# Champions rules evidence is integrity-checked byte-for-byte against hashes
# stored in rules.snapshot.json. Never let Windows checkout/autocrlf rewrite
# these archived evidence bytes, or NEW MATCH will correctly fail closed with
# RULES_SNAPSHOT_EVIDENCE_HASH_MISMATCH on an otherwise clean checkout.
src/maple_next/data/champions_rules/**/evidence/*.html -text
